Article 13 (Fees)
(1) Fees for granting fixed dates and providing information shall be as follows: <Amended on May 25, 2017>
1. Granting fee: 600 won per case (an additional 100 won for every four pages exceeding four pages of the housing lease contract);
2. Information-provision fee: 600 won per case (an additional 50 won for each page exceeding 10 pages of output): Provided, That amounts of less than 100 won shall be disregarded when calculating fees, and where a printed document is provided simultaneously with inspection, no separate inspection fee shall be charged;
3. Where an application for an electronic fixed date or request for provision of information is made through the Internet Registry Office, the fee shall be 500 won for each, and additional fees under subparagraphs 1 and 2 shall not apply: Provided, That where fixed-date information is requested in combination with inspection of registration records through the Internet Registry Office, the information-provision fee may be reduced or exempted as prescribed by Supreme Court Regulation.
(2) Where a lessee falls under any of the following, the fees under paragraph (1) shall be exempted: Provided, That this shall not apply where an application for an electronic fixed date or request for provision of information is made through the Internet Registry Office:
1. A recipient under Article 2, subparagraph 2 of the National Basic Living Security Act;
2. A patriot of independence or bereaved family member registered under Article 6 of the Act on the Honorable Treatment of Persons of Distinguished Service to Independence (limited to the person with first priority);
3. A person of distinguished service to the State or bereaved family member registered under Article 6 of the Act on the Honorable Treatment of and Support for Persons of Distinguished Service to the State (limited to the person with first priority);
4. A patient suffering from aftereffects of defoliants, a patient suffering from aftereffects of defoliants, or a second-generation patient registered under Article 4 of the Act on Support for Patients Suffering from Aftereffects of Defoliants and Establishment of Related Associations;
5. A person of distinguished service in war registered under Article 5 of the Act on Honorable Treatment of Persons of Distinguished Service in War and Establishment of Related Associations;
6. A person of distinguished service to the May 18 Democratization Movement or bereaved family member determined for registration under Article 7 of the Act on the Honorable Treatment of Persons of Distinguished Service to the May 18 Democratization Movement (limited to the person with first priority);
7. A person of distinguished service for special missions or bereaved family member registered under Article 6 of the Act on Honorable Treatment of Persons of Distinguished Service for Special Missions and Establishment of Related Associations (limited to the person with first priority);
8. A person wounded in an act of righteousness or bereaved family member of a person who died in an act of righteousness recognized under Article 5 of the Act on Honorable Treatment of and Support for Persons Who Died or Were Injured for Public Good (limited to the person with first priority);
9. A person eligible for protection under Article 5 of the Single-Parent Family Support Act;
10. Other persons prescribed by Supreme Court Regulation in circumstances equivalent to those under the preceding subparagraphs.
